# ImageGalleryService Documentation

A high-performance Flutter image gallery service with AI-powered tagging, pagination, and thumbnail management.

## 🚀 Quick Start

```dart
// Initialize service
final galleryService = ImageGalleryService();
await galleryService.init(enableAITagging: true);

// Add folders
await galleryService.addFolder('/storage/Pictures', enableAITagging: true);

// Load images (paginated)
final result = await galleryService.getImages(page: 0, pageSize: 50);

// Get thumbnail path for display
final thumbnail = await galleryService.getThumbnailPath(imageId, 'medium');
```

## 📋 Core Methods

### Initialization

```dart
Future<void> init({bool enableAITagging = false})
```

Initialize database and thumbnail directory. Must be called first.

### Folder Management

```dart
// Add folder for scanning
Future<int> addFolder(String folderPath, {String? customName, bool enableAITagging = false})

// Get all folders with image counts
Future<List<Folder>> getAllFolders()

// Scan existing folder
Future<void> scanFolder(int folderId, {bool enableAITagging = false})

// Remove folder and all its images
Future<void> removeFolder(int folderId)
```

