## 🔍 4. Filters and Queries

You can do **powerful filters** easily:

```ts
const users = await prisma.user.findMany({
  where: {
    isActive: true,
    email: { contains: '@gmail.com' },
    createdAt: { gte: new Date('2025-01-01') },
  },
  orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
  take: 10, // LIMIT 10
  skip: 5,  // OFFSET 5
});
```

---

## 🧩 5. Relations (Joins)

If you defined relations (like `User` → `Post`), you can fetch related data:

```ts
const userWithPosts = await prisma.user.findUnique({
  where: { id: 1 },
  include: { posts: true },
});
```

Or just select specific parts:

```ts
const post = await prisma.post.findUnique({
  where: { id: 1 },
  select: {
    title: true,
    author: { select: { name: true, email: true } },
  },
});
```

---

## 🛠 6. Transactions

To ensure multiple operations succeed together (or fail together):

```ts
await prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
  const user = await tx.user.create({ data: { ... } });
  await tx.post.create({ data: { authorId: user.id, ... } });
});
```

---

## 🧱 7. Aggregates and Counts

```ts
const userCount = await prisma.user.count({
  where: { isActive: true },
});

const avgPosts = await prisma.post.aggregate({
  _avg: { id: true },
});
```

